#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Box is the one block for every surface on a page. Pick what it is — a plain wrapper, a card, a panel, a cover, a badge, a divider or a spacer — and how it arranges what's inside: one under another, side by side, in even columns, or layered on top of each other. Each choice is a starting point that sets ordinary style values, so everything it sets can be changed in the Style tab."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "What the box is. Plain has no look of its own; Card, Panel and Cover start from a framed, tinted or full-color look and hold other blocks; Badge holds a short line of text; Divider draws a line; Spacer is empty room. Picking another kind starts its look over. A badge, divider or spacer holds no blocks, so those are offered only while the box is empty."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Stores the full Blicks style tree. Arrangement, width, height and \"stay on screen\" all write into it."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "The element the box is, for search engines and screen readers: a section of the page, a card or post, a side note, navigation and so on. It does not change the look."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Set by the \"On top\" arrangement: every child shares one cell, so later ones sit over earlier ones — words over a picture."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "The label a badge shows."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Makes the whole box clickable. A container box gets a link stretched over it, with links and buttons inside it still clickable; a badge becomes the link."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Use a Card arranged as a stack inside a Grid box for pricing and feature cards."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Use Section for page bands, including anything that runs edge to edge (full-bleed); a Box stays within the content width. Put Boxes inside the Section."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "A Cover arranged \"On top\" puts a heading over a background picture."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "Button renders a clickable action. It can output a real button when no URL is set or a link-style button when a URL is provided."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "The visible button label."
msgstr ""

#: build/block-library.js:1
#: build/editor.js:1
msgid "The destination URL. When set, the block renders as an anchor so it can navigate like a link."
